-# Etymology rows of the two protonym forms (edit protonym; new taxon with a new protonym).
-# Locals: f (form builder for the protonym), protonym, name_prefix ("protonym" or
-# "taxon[protonym_attributes]"), id_prefix ("protonym" or "taxon_protonym_attributes").
%tr
  %td
    =f.label :etymology do
      Etymology (verbatim)
      =db_tooltip_icon :etymology, scope: :protonyms
  %td
    =render 'taxt_editors/field_taxt_editor', name: "#{name_prefix}[etymology_taxt]", content: protonym.etymology_taxt
    .text-sm
      The author's words exactly as printed, in the original language; nothing added or changed. Needs a source
      and a page. AntCat's own reading goes in "AntCat derivation", never here.
%tr
  %td
    =f.label :etymology_source do
      Etymology source
      =db_tooltip_icon :etymology_source, scope: :protonyms
  %td
    =f.select :etymology_source, Protonym::ETYMOLOGY_SOURCES.invert, include_blank: '(blank)'
    .text-sm
      Original description: the reference is the authorship reference, so leave the reference below blank.
      Later work: pick its reference below.
%tr
  %td
    =f.label :etymology_reference_id do
      Etymology reference (later work only)
  %td=reference_picker protonym.etymology_reference, name: "#{name_prefix}[etymology_reference_id]", id: "#{id_prefix}_etymology_reference_id"
%tr
  %td
    =f.label :etymology_pages do
      Etymology page(s)
  %td
    .max-w-xs=f.text_field :etymology_pages
%tr
  %td
    =f.label :etymology_translation do
      Etymology translation (AntCat)
  %td
    =f.text_area :etymology_translation, rows: 2
    .text-sm English, only when the original is not in English. Shown as AntCat's translation.
%tr
  %td
    =f.label :etymology_derivation do
      AntCat derivation
      =db_tooltip_icon :etymology_derivation, scope: :protonyms
  %td
    =f.text_area :etymology_derivation, rows: 2
    .text-sm
      AntCat's own reading of the name (for example Latin crassus, thick, + spina, spine), where the author
      gave none or to add to it. Always shown as AntCat's, never as the author's.
